<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>

<chapter xml:id="ch-differentiation-i" xmlns:xi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XInclude">
  <title>Differentiation I</title>

  <introduction>
    <p>
        Differentiation is the study of how functions change, and has applications in fields such as physics, engineering, and economics.
    </p>
    <p>
        In this chapter, we will introduce the concept of differentiation. We will start by looking at average rates of change and then move on to introducing the derivative. We will also look at how to find the derivative graphically and how to use derivatives to find equations of gradients and normals. Finally, we will look at some applications of derivatives in kinematics and real life.
    </p>
  </introduction>

